      <Placemark>
        <name>Teshuvah Ministries	Isaac and Rebekah Garvin</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Description: Address: 311 E Coeur Dalene Ave C2	Coeur d Alene	ID	83815<br>Email: repent@teshuvahministries.com<br>Phone: (208) 651-2531<br>Website: www.teshuvahministries.com<br>Comments: We are a ministry that is mostly producing web-based materials for the Scattered (teaching videos, articles etc). But we do have a small and growing brick-n-morter / online store where materials and our Feast Packets are available for purchase. As well as a small lending library in our office in downtown CDA. Rebekah travels to teach the Ladies of Teshuvah Workshops and is available to speak and present this Workshop during your Sukkot. We have a monthly Youth Group Activity and Pizza on the New Moons and are seeking to establish a Youth Summer Camp here in Idaho. The mission of Teshuvah Ministries is to walk in step with Rabbi Yahshua and promote a simple understanding of the Melchizedek Priesthood and what it means to repent and return.<br>Coordinates: -116.7520948,47.6684721,0]]></description>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value><![CDATA[Address: 311 E Coeur Dalene Ave C2	Coeur d Alene	ID	83815<br>Email: repent@teshuvahministries.com<br>Phone: (208) 651-2531<br>Website: www.teshuvahministries.com<br>Comments: We are a ministry that is mostly producing web-based materials for the Scattered (teaching videos, articles etc). But we do have a small and growing brick-n-morter / online store where materials and our Feast Packets are available for purchase. As well as a small lending library in our office in downtown CDA. Rebekah travels to teach the Ladies of Teshuvah Workshops and is available to speak and present this Workshop during your Sukkot. We have a monthly Youth Group Activity and Pizza on the New Moons and are seeking to establish a Youth Summer Camp here in Idaho. The mission of Teshuvah Ministries is to walk in step with Rabbi Yahshua and promote a simple understanding of the Melchizedek Priesthood and what it means to repent and return.]]></value>
